# 0096-gpu-without-bc-textures.patch -- older iPhones and iPads (a GPU without BC textures: before the A17 Pro, the M1) play: the chain decodes the textures on the CPU, and the app says so.
# Applies after 0095.
# UNTESTED ON DEVICE AND IN THE SIMULATOR (a simulator's GPU has BC textures): compiled, and its pure part ran in the host harness (below).
#
# The shim asks Metal once (gameapp_gpu_bc_textures: MTLCreateSystemDefaultDevice().supportsBCTextureCompression, 1 / 0 / -1) and hands the chain IBUILDER_FLAG_GPU_NO_BC; every boot then
# sets DM_PROF_TEX_BC_CPU=1, which the host reads on top of its profile (hle_profile.c read_env) so nvn_mtl.m decodes BC1-7 on the CPU (nvn_bcdec.c) instead of stopping at mtl_init
# ("has no BC texture formats"). The chain logs "GPU without BC textures: textures decoded on the CPU (slower, more memory)". On a GPU with BC textures nothing changes.
# The app, on such a device only:
#   * Settings › This iPhone (the Keys page): "Textures  decoded on the CPU — this GPU has no BC support (slower, more memory)";
#   * a game's sheet: an info row "Textures · Decoded on the CPU" with one line of explanation;
#   * the first build: one notice, "This GPU has no BC textures … performance may be low …" (Documents/gameapp.settings.tsv keeps cpu_textures_notice 1).
#
# VERIFIED: see 0095 (the same compile and harness runs cover both).
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on a device without BC textures (an A16 or older iPhone): the real speed and memory of the CPU decode, the Metal query on such a GPU.
# NEW UI STRINGS: "Textures: decoded on the CPU — this GPU has no BC support", "This GPU has no BC textures", "Decoded on the CPU"; settings key "cpu_textures_notice".
